{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The monitor mount fits my effort to free desk space: my cable organizers and under-desk headphone holder suggest that making my computer setup tidier matters to me.",
    "The battery backup offers a useful next step for my computer setup because it could give me time to save work during a brief outage, provided its capacity is sufficient."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The wireless adapter addresses a need I have already covered with my recent Ethernet adapter and cables; being another networking accessory does not make it useful right now.",
    "The Lightning cable assumes a compatible device I have not shown I own, while the photo frame and smart speakers serve purposes I am not currently pursuing.",
    "More wired headphones and Ethernet cables fit my interests, but I would pass because I already have several headphones and just bought a five-pack of cables."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases of computer accessories seem to have been taken as interest in almost any electronic device, even when it serves a different purpose.",
    "Past purchases of headphones, cables and memory cards seem to be treated as reasons to buy more without enough attention to whether I still need them."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases often complete a setup, so I am more interested in something that solves a remaining problem than something that repeats a purchase.",
    "Compatibility matters before I choose: I would need to check the monitor mount fit, supported memory-card capacity and battery-backup capacity.",
    "An item can match my interests without being something I would choose now; a longer cable or larger memory card needs a specific use to justify it."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical computer-setup interests but miss the distinction between useful additions, needs already met and devices I have no current reason to buy."
}"}
